    "result_text": "All 55 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a structured address form to the Spring PetClinic owner-creation flow, keeping the flat `address` input backward-compatible.\n\n**OpenAPI schema** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 DTOs are generated from it at build time):\n- Added optional `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` properties to the `OwnerFields` schema (inherited by the `Owner` response schema via `allOf`).\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list so a structured-only request is accepted; the flat `address` doubles as the composed output field.\n\n**Model** (`Owner.java`): added `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` fields (columns `address_line1`, `address_line2`) with getters/setters. MapStruct maps them automatically by name in both directions.\n\n**DB schemas**: added `address_line1`/`address_line2` columns to hsqldb (used by tests), h2, mysql, and postgres.\n\n**Controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n- `applyAddress(owner)` prefers the structured fields when `addressLine1` is non-blank: it normalizes `addressLine1` and (when present) `addressLine2` with the existing `normalizeAddress` logic (upper-case, whitespace collapse, `ST\u2192STREET` etc.), and composes `address` = normalized `addressLine1` + (` ` + normalized `addressLine2` when present). Otherwise it clears the structured lines and normalizes the flat `address` alone.\n- `rejectMissingOrBlankFields` now requires an address in *either* form (non-blank `addressLine1` or non-blank flat `address`) plus city.\n\nThe reads that consume city/postcode (household hash, postcode validation, locality) already draw on the shared top-level fields, which are identical across both address forms, so their behaviour is unchanged.\n\nAll existing and new tests (including `Cp01`, `Cp12`, `Cp44`) are green.",
